%% Source basis: Lecture 4 and Intel MCS-51 User's Manual [2]
flowchart LR
    CALL[CALL from ordinary program] --> PUSH1[push return PC]
    PUSH1 --> SUB[ordinary subroutine]
    SUB --> RET[RET]
    RET --> POP1[pop PC]
    POP1 --> MAIN1[resume caller]
    EVENT[eligible hardware event] --> HLCALL[hardware-generated LCALL]
    HLCALL --> PUSH2[push interrupted PC]
    PUSH2 --> ISR[interrupt service routine]
    ISR --> RETI[RETI]
    RETI --> STATE[mark current interrupt complete\nallow same-level acceptance per architecture]
    STATE --> POP2[pop PC]
    POP2 --> MAIN2[resume interrupted program]
    BAD[plain RET at end of ISR] --> WRONG[PC may return, but interrupt-control state\nmay still regard interrupt as in progress]
